*> GO TO out of a performed range. Jumps inside the range, to an exit
*> that ends the run, and to code that falls into STOP RUN are fine.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. LEAVES.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  EOF-FLAG           PIC X VALUE "N".
01  COUNTER            PIC 9(4) VALUE 0.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    PERFORM READ-RECORD THRU READ-EXIT
    PERFORM COUNT-RECORD
    PERFORM CHECK-SECTION
    GO TO FINISH.
READ-RECORD.
    IF EOF-FLAG = "Y"
        GO TO READ-EXIT
    END-IF
    IF COUNTER > 9000
        GO TO ABEND-EXIT
    END-IF
    IF COUNTER = 0
        GO TO MAIN-LINE
    END-IF.
READ-EXIT.
    EXIT.
COUNT-RECORD.
    ADD 1 TO COUNTER
    IF COUNTER > 100
        GO TO SUMMARY
    END-IF.
SUMMARY.
    DISPLAY COUNTER
    GO TO FINISH.
ABEND-EXIT.
    DISPLAY "ABEND"
    STOP RUN.
CHECK-SECTION SECTION.
CHECK-START.
    IF COUNTER = 1
        GO TO CHECK-END
    END-IF
    GO TO OTHER-SECTION.
CHECK-END.
    EXIT.
OTHER-SECTION SECTION.
FINISH.
    DISPLAY "DONE".
LAST-STEP.
    STOP RUN.
